{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110360","id":2812992944,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6nqt2w","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110360","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110360.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110360.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110360","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110360/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110360/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110360/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/e5ab5acd95e871d0c8093d5d0fb10111a6891dbe","number":110360,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Rename `RDD::MemoryBarrier` to avoid conflicts with the Windows headers.","user":{"login":"zorbathut","id":160754,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MDc1NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/160754?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zorbathut","html_url":"https://github.com/zorbathut","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zorbathut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zorbathut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zorbathut/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zorbathut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zorbathut/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zorbathut/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zorbathut/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zorbathut/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zorbathut/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"TL;DR at the bottom.\r\n\r\nLong explanation: The Windows headers `#define MemoryBarrier __faststorefence` on AMD64, and this causes problems with a struct defined in RenderingDeviceDriver, also named MemoryBarrier. We've got some workarounds for this (`#undef MemoryBarrier` in typedefs.h, rendering_device_driver_d3d12.h, and rendering_shader_container_d3d12.cpp) but these are unfortunately insufficient. The issue is that there are *many* orders that things can happen; for example:\r\n\r\n* Include rendering_device_driver.h, which creates a struct named MemoryBarrier\r\n* Include typedefs.h, which include-guards itself and will not work a second time\r\n* Include windows.h, which redefines MemoryBarrier as __faststorefence\r\n* Now if you try to use MemoryBarrier you get confusing errors about __faststorefence and there's no good way to fix it because typedefs.h has already been used\r\n\r\nOr the opposite:\r\n\r\n* Include typedefs.h, which include-guards itself and will not work a second time\r\n* Include windows.h, which redefines MemoryBarrier as __faststorefence\r\n* Include rendering_device_driver.h, which creates a struct named __faststorefence\r\n* Include rendering_device_driver_d3d12.h, which undefines MemoryBarrier\r\n* Now if you try to use MemoryBarrier you get confusing errors about MemoryBarrier being missing because it was misnamed to start with\r\n\r\nIt's worth noting that this problem exists in the current codebase. Find `struct MemoryBarrier {`, add this before it:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\n#ifdef MemoryBarrier\r\n#error MemoryBarrier has been defined by Windows.\r\n#endif\r\n```\r\n\r\nand build on Windows. The build will break. Turns out the current codebase is mostly working out of accident; a good number of files are being built with the wrong struct name, but we're always using it in an order that happens to function properly within a single translation unit.\r\n\r\nThere isn't really a great way to solve this. We could try to require that every place including windows.h goes through our own header that applies the #undef. We could add undefs *everywhere that uses MemoryBarrier*. We could have a `remove_windows_defines.h` that doesn't include-guard itself so we can include it everywhere. These are all ugly. Instead we can just rename MemoryBarrier. This is unfortunate because MemoryBarrier is a really good term. I've chosen MemoryAccessBarrier as the least-bad alternative I could come up with; I am happy to change this to anything else, just lemme know.\r\n\r\nI ran into this problem *a ton* when working on LibGodot functionality and my eventual solution was kind of a nuclear solution, but it burned a few hours of work in the process as I fought with it. This is an attempt to get a cleaner solution that I can build on for a future pull request, and to save future developers from burning their own few hours.\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\nTL;DR. This change:\r\n\r\n* renames Godot's RDD::MemoryBarrier to RDD::MemoryAccessBarrier\r\n* removes the #undef's for MemoryBarrier since they are no longer needed\r\n* does not change the thirdparty vulkan library which uses the same token name, I assume they've solved this their own way","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":205417413,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMDU0MTc0MTM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:windows","name":"platform:windows","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12939969,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AxXLB","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23","html_url":